(6964039, 1048138, 119419, '<td valign="top">Iconic and speaks volumes of the documentation of human endevour. "The known is finite, the unknown infinite; intellectually we stand on an islet in the midst of an illimitable ocean of inexplicability. Our business in every generation is to reclaim a little more land, to add something to the extent and the solidity of our possessions." <i>Thomas Henry Huxley - On the Reception of the Origin of Species (1887)</i>. You have done your bit ;)</td>', 'Iconic and speaks volumes of the documentation of human endevour. "The known is finite, the unknown infinite; intellectually we stand on an islet in the midst of an illimitable ocean of inexplicability. Our business in every generation is to reclaim a little more land, to add something to the extent and the solidity of our possessions." Thomas Henry Huxley - On the Reception of the Origin of Species (1887). You have done your bit ;)', '2013-01-24 23:53:07.000000', NULL, 0),
